## Band: present

<section name="present" heading='SectionHeading "Verb Conjugation" (subtitle "Present tense — the ending shows who is doing the action")'>

### Start Here: είμαι (to be)

<paradigm name="eimai" highlight="true" eyebrow="Start here">
<verb>είμαι</verb>
<meaning>am, is, are</meaning>
<note>The most common Greek verb. Memorise it first.</note>
<note>3rd person is the same for singular and plural</note>

| Person       | Singular  | Plural    |
|--------------|-----------|-----------|
| 1st          | είμαι     | είμαστε   |
| 2nd          | είσαι     | είστε     |
| 3rd          | είναι     | είναι     |

</paradigm>

### Pattern Identifier

<decision-guide name="pattern-identifier" component="PatternIdentifier">
<question>Which pattern? Look at the verb's dictionary form (1st person singular)</question>

| Ending    | Pattern Name | Examples                |
|-----------|--------------|-------------------------|
| -ω        | Active       | κάνω, θέλω, βλέπω       |
| -άω/-ώ    | Contracted   | μιλάω, αγαπάω           |
| -μαι      | Deponent     | έρχομαι, θυμάμαι        |

</decision-guide>

<note name="negation">
**Negation:** put δεν before any verb: Δεν μιλάω (I don't speak)
</note>

### Side by Side: "Same slots, different endings"

`PatternComparison`: one table, person rows (I, you, he/she, we, you all, they) x the three canonical verbs, stem neutral and ending in the family colour.

### Pattern 1: Active -ω

<paradigm name="active" scheme="verb-active">
<pattern>-ω</pattern>
<description>Most Greek verbs follow this pattern. Learn the endings once, apply them to thousands of verbs.</description>

| Person | Singular      | Plural        |
|--------|---------------|---------------|
| 1st    | κάν**ω**      | κάν**ουμε**   |
| 2nd    | κάν**εις**    | κάν**ετε**    |
| 3rd    | κάν**ει**     | κάν**ουν**    |

Same pattern (collapsible): θέλω, έχω, βλέπω, δουλεύω, μένω, ακούω, παίρνω, ξέρω
See it in action (collapsible): Τι κάνεις; · Κάνει κρύο. · Κάνουμε διάλειμμα.
</paradigm>

### Pattern 2: Contracted -άω/-ώ

<paradigm name="contracted" scheme="verb-contracted">
<pattern>-άω/-ώ</pattern>
<description>Stress falls on the ending, not the stem. Both -άω and -ώ spellings are correct: μιλάω = μιλώ.</description>

| Person | Singular      | Plural        |
|--------|---------------|---------------|
| 1st    | μιλ**άω**     | μιλ**άμε**    |
| 2nd    | μιλ**άς**     | μιλ**άτε**    |
| 3rd    | μιλ**άει**    | μιλ**άνε**    |

Same pattern: αγαπάω, ρωτάω, περνάω
See it in action: Μιλάς ελληνικά; · Δεν μιλάμε πολύ.
Footer: the -ώ variant (μπορώ, οδηγώ) has different endings, shown in "Other high-frequency verbs".
</paradigm>

### Pattern 3: Deponent -μαι

<paradigm name="deponent" scheme="verb-deponent">
<pattern>-μαι</pattern>
<description>These verbs end in -μαι but have active meaning. Two variants: -ομαι (έρχομαι) and -άμαι (θυμάμαι). Memorise as units.</description>

| Person | Singular        | Plural          |
|--------|-----------------|-----------------|
| 1st    | έρχ**ομαι**     | ερχ**όμαστε**   |
| 2nd    | έρχ**εσαι**     | έρχ**εστε**     |
| 3rd    | έρχ**εται**     | έρχ**ονται**    |

Same pattern: γίνομαι, θυμάμαι, κάθομαι
See it in action: Έρχομαι αύριο. · Πότε έρχεσαι; · Δεν θυμάμαι.
</paradigm>

### Other High-Frequency Verbs (MemoriseCard, honey)

<section name="irregulars">
<note>These don't follow the 3 patterns. Memorise as units. Rows are IRREGULAR_VERBS minus είμαι.</note>

| Verb  | Forms (sg1 sg2 sg3 / pl1 pl2 pl3)                       | Note                              |
|-------|---------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| μπορώ | μπορώ μπορείς μπορεί / μπορούμε μπορείτε μπορούν        | Always followed by να             |
| λέω   | λέω λές λέει / λέμε λέτε λένε                           | "τα λέμε" = see you later         |
| τρώω  | τρώω τρώς τρώει / τρώμε τρώτε τρώνε                     |                                   |
| πάω   | πάω πάς πάει / πάμε πάτε πάνε                           | Alternative regular form: πηγαίνω |

</section>

Cross-link card: "Browse all verbs, irregulars first" → /learn/verbs.
</section>

